# Velocity by hand (0.15.23): on JAM, SEL held makes a key an accent (and not the shift); an Akai MPK mini (MIDI IN's Notes: MPK): its keys play the
# JAM page's voice with their velocity, its pads (channel 10) are the pads' bank A, its knobs (CC 70-77) and mod wheel (CC 1) the FX knobs, the
# acid, bass and reverb, and the mood. The pluck's MIDI out shows the velocity: 40 + 87 x the level (a plain key 0.95: 122, an accent 127).
seed 0
wait 3000
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 0
tap GLO
wait 100
spin SELECT 1
wait 100
spin SELECT 1
wait 200
expect view 33
expect jamv 0
key 5 down
wait 100
expect lastvel 122
key 5 up
wait 100
press SEL
wait 100
key 7 down
wait 100
expect lastvel 127
key 7 up
release SEL
wait 100
expect view 33
# the MPK on MIDI IN
press HOME
wait 900
release HOME
wait 100
turn SELECT 3
wait 100
expect fxpage 26
spin K1 1
wait 100
spin K1 1
wait 100
spin K1 1
wait 200
expect minpads 3
shot midiin_mpk.png
# a key at velocity 64: the pluck at 0.95 x 0.64
midi 90 3C 40
wait 100
expect lastvel 92
midi 80 3C 00
# a key on the MPK (and a chord's notes let go with it)
tap PLAY
wait 300
# pad 9 (bank B's first, note 44 on channel 10): the breakdown on the bar
midi 99 2C 64
wait 2500
expect sec 1
# the knobs: the first (CC 70) the filter right down, the mod wheel the mood
midi B0 46 00
midi B0 01 7F
wait 100
expect fxk0 -50
expect mood 100
# kept
wait 6000
reboot
wait 3000
expect minpads 3
